WEBVTT

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.850
Hello, is this the telegraph office?

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.600
I'd like to send an express message to Tokyo.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.220
The address is, uh...

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.110
Tokyo City, Bunkyo Ward, Koraku 1-3,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.120
Korakuen Hall, Waiting Room, Yabuki Joe and Mr. Nishi Kanichi.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.970
And as for the telegram...

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.450
H-Hold on a second.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.400
Hey, which one do I send?

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.910
Well, you see...

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.770
We talked it over with everyone last night...

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.130
but we couldn't make a decision, so... Can I grab that?

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.410
Hey, Mr. Telegram Man.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.900
The guy we're sending the telegram to has vowed to invade...

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.090
I mean, break into a new world, where the sun shines, so...

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.640
Okay, let me just get on with it.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.560
So should we say "beat it"... or "good job"?

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:11.150
Okay, let's go with the one that sounds friendlier! Make the telegram say "good job"!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.070
Is Yabuki the contender here?

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.150
You have a telegram! A telegram!

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.620
For me?

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.450
Hup!

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.600
Who's it from?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.410
It says...

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:41.140
"We wish you the best of fortune in your new season of life - Nogiku Island Juvenile Prison."

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.570
But that's a wedding greeting!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.310
Joe...

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.310
Come to think of it, Skeleton Boy is still there!

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.380
I can't think of anyone but him who would come up with something this wacky.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.730
Man, he must have been out of his gourd.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.490
He's the son of a bath house owner, and he got thrown into juvie for peeping on all the women.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:16.230
Joe!

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.170
You should probably stop chattering now.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.240
Nishi's match is coming up. Put his gloves on for him.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.350
Okay, then! Let's see, the gloves...

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.310
Hey, Nishi!

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.240
Where'd you put the bag with your gloves?

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.340
Listen, Nishi.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.250
Four rounds will fly by sooner than you think.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.450
So instead of analyzing your opponent's moves,

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.250
you should start the match at your own pace.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:48.850
Yes.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.910
This may be asking too much, considering it's your first match and all...

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.020
If you stiffen up, you'll lose.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.560
Relax, as if you're practicing.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.320
Right.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.320
Got it.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.470
Hey, Nishi!

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:08.830
How was that?

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.450
Now you've stopped trembling.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.960
I-It stopped!

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.020
Okay, that's good!

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.280
Now, let's put our hands together,

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.130
and pray for Mammoth Nishi's victory!

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:21.940
Ready...

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.320
Hey, you! The noisy guy!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.470
Let me remind you that this isn't your private waiting room.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:34.440
Could you please stop all that yelling and humming in this crowded space?

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.950
You gotta have etiquette in this shared place!

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:43.450
All the fighters are trying to calm down before their matches!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.410
Don't you think dead silence would make it harder to calm down?

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:49.910
What?

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.230
The way you guys looked earlier...

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:57.580
you looked as pathetic as prisoners the day before their executions!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.920
What was that, you bastard!?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.420
Hey, cut it out, Joe!

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.070
I apologize for the trouble.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.430
This guy's just agitated because today's his first match.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.930
Who did you say is agitated?

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.930
Shut up, you asshole!

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.630
He's scary!

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:22.520
Sorry for being so loud...

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.820
Mammoth Nishi, your match is up.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.320
Get to the ring.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.500
He'll be there shortly.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:32.320
Well then, Joe, I'll be going as Nishi's second,

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.890
so you'd better behave here.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.370
Come on, Nishi. Let's go.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.370
Hang on...

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.520
That's just not fair!

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:43.880
This is the debut match of my friend who trained with me!

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.120
Let me be his second, okay, old man?

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:46.690
Let me be his second, okay, old man?

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:47.740
Joe!

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:51.570
You can't be a second with your temperament.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.390
If you get too excited on the ringside, you'll confuse Nishi.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.850
I-I'll be fine, Joe...

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.350
Wh-What do you mean, you'll be...

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.310
Now, stay inside, rest, and behave!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.750
Well, do your best out there!

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.370
Make sure you live up to the name of Mammoth Nishi!

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:13.370
Leave this to me!

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.390
I'll score the first victory for Tange Gym,

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.870
and give you good luck for your debut match!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.370
Hurry, hurry!

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.330
The first victory...

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.750
You can do it, Nishi!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.970
So that one-eyed man's their only second...

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.680
What a surprise. Is he gonna take care of both of them on his own?

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.610
I've never heard of a pro only having one second during a match!

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.870
Hey, you! Baldy masseur!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.870
Baldy masseur?

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.370
Let me just remind you that this isn't your private waiting room.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.340
So would you please stop gossiping?

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.380
K-Kid...

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.180
Come on, it's nothing to get mad over!

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:12.890
I'm just telling you what you told me.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:20.000
I'm trying to calm down before my match here.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.590
Despicable brat!

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.520
This is my first match as a pro...

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.580
Three cheers for Yabuki Joe!

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.620
Joe! Congratulations on becoming a pro!

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.370
Do your best!

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.210
Go for it, Joe!

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:47.750
Everyone's gonna be watching me.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.550
I have to do my best.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:57.180
What the...

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.260
D-Did you lose, Nishi?

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:07.190
My eyelid got cut, and my opponent kept aiming for my wound,

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.360
and I lost by TKO.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.170
Stop talking and lay down!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.740
Hey, Joe!

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.730
Don't just stand there! Get your gloves on!

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:30.670
You're up next!

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.300
Y-Yeah...

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:37.680
Joe...

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.680
Yeah?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:45.640
Be careful. A pro match is tougher than I'd expected.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.100
It's really terrifying...

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.690
Don't get gloomy on me, Nishi.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.650
You could've won if you hadn't gotten injured.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.490
You heard the man, Nishi.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.160
Don't worry. I'll make up for your loss.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.410
Yabuki Joe.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.410
Your match is up.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.420
Get to the ring.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:10.420
Get to the ring.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:14.420
Get to the ring.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.600
All right, let's go, old man!

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.430
Okay! Let's move out!

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.300
Joe, you finally made it.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.130
Yeah. Somehow.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.560
At the top of these stairs...

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.230
your tomorrow...

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.780
<i>our</i> tomorrow awaits.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:15.700
Tomorrow...

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.630
I may have yelled at you back there...

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:29.210
but you have no idea how happy I am now, Joe.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.790
Thank you so much for walking this far with me.

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:34.840
And...

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.900
Congratulations on your debut.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:44.540
Why do you old guys have to be so square and formal at times like this, Tange-kun?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.740
T-Tange-kun!?

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.350
T-Tange-kun!?

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.760
Now, let's go, old man.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:56.980
Yeah! Let's go!

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:40.130
Old man, it's kinda... bright!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.130
Old man, it's kinda... bright!

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.410
Joe...

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:44.610
I feel the same.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:05.430
<i>We will now hold the opening match for the six-round bantamweight class!</i>

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:11.120
<i>In the red corner, from Kitaboshi Gym,</i>

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.530
<i>weighing in at 118 pounds...</i>

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.460
<i>Murase Takeo!</i>

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.350
<i>And in the blue corner...</i>

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:28.900
<i>from Tange Boxing Club...</i>

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:36.430
<i>weighing in at 117 and a half pounds...</i>

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.440
<i>Yabuki Joe!</i>

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.940
I've been waiting for this!

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:47.950
Show us how you fight!

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.860
Yeah! Go wild!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:52.330
We all came to see you!

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:53.910
Show us a real fight!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.480
Win!

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:56.910
Do your best!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.200
Bro really is amazing...

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:00.200
<i>I never thought he'd be this popular...</i>

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:01.240
Amazing!

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.560
Now this is a surprise!

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:08.210
The crowd's going wild as if this were a world title match!

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:13.020
I don't think the audience has ever reacted to a debut match in such a manner before!

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:17.200
Yabuki the contender and Coach Tange are standing dumbfounded in the corner!

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.010
Joe!

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:19.930
H-Hey!

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.440
Y-Yeah...

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:25.400
S-Say something to them!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.990
Everyone came to see you!

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:31.480
Me?

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:36.500
Don't you get it? This is your night!

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:38.610
Mine?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.730
My night?

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:43.590
Mine...

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:49.270
Don't just stand there, you idiot!

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:50.760
Say something!

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:51.490
Go, go!

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:57.340
Joe!

00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:58.770
You look really cool when you're all flustered!

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.910
Idiot! Stop scratching your head!

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.470
Don't be scared, just wave!

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:08.440
Well then...

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.990
Way to go!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.800
Give us a good fight!

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:21.290
All this cheering is making me feel happy!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.580
All right!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.380
Yahoo!

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:25.380
Yay!

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.210
Hey, Joe! That's enough!

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:43.270
Yabuki Joe is blowing kisses to his cheering fans in the middle of the ring!

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.970
Still, he seems pretty popular, right?

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:49.320
Yeah. The media really made a fuss about him and puffed him up.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:55.120
But I bet that Murase-kun with his longer career will punch out that puffed-up head.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.130
He's acting like a star.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.880
I still can't tell if he's just acting as a star, or if he really is a star.

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.850
That son of a bitch is getting carried away!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.060
No, Wolf! Don't get up!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:23.730
But that attitude of his makes me want to throw up!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:27.600
Don't be hasty, Wolf. Save your anger.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:30.730
You won't be sitting and twiddling your thumbs forever.

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:31.960
Come on!

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:37.740
Moron! Don't get cocky, you attention whore!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:42.200
Save the flashy act for after you've beaten Murase!

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:44.550
What are you talking about?

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:45.930
I've practically won already!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:46.710
What?

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:50.710
That Murase's no big deal, after all.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:52.630
Stop bragging!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.770
Unlike you, who went straight to the B-class test,

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:59.380
he's a veteran that fought through plenty of four-round matches!

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.420
Well, if he fought so many four-round matches...

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.730
and still got his nose so deformed...

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.730
he must suck at defense.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.180
What a guy.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:16.410
He doesn't know anything about the theory of boxing...

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.700
but what he just said is correct.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:22.090
He really is proving himself to be a natural boxer.

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:25.370
Old man, at any rate I'm gonna do it.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.710
Old man, at any rate I'm gonna do it.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:29.120
I'll fight a good match.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.630
Because we've got some familiar faces in the crowd.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:40.220
I don't want to give him a bad fight.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:42.360
Joe...

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.320
It's not just Rikiishi.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.270
All the guys from skid row are here, too.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.770
I know, I know.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.690
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:55.690
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:02.450
Well, old man...

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.020
I'm off.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:20.960
A rush! A rush!

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:21.840
Murase's rushing him!

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.730
He's started a savage rush just as the bell rung!

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.360
Yabuki can't do a thing!

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:27.890
He's already on the defensive!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.230
I'll show you...

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.570
which one of us...

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.060
has a bad defense!

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:37.610
Oh? You heard me?

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:38.530
Shut up!

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.430
You're about to learn that your stupid street boxing...

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:48.960
won't get you anywhere in the world of pros!

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:55.420
And Murase hit him with a powerful right straight! And a left! Right!

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.420
And he's hit him again! Murase's got his chance!

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:00.430
Joe, go around him!

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:02.430
Idiot, go around him, Joe!

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.850
Yabuki-kun! Do your best!

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.430
Joe! Hang in there!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.170
Bro Joe!

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:10.010
Yabuki-kun, what the hell...

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:12.440
This is no time to goof off!

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.520
Come on, it was only a Joe-ke.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:16.440
Hey!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:16.440
<i>Ouch!</i>

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:19.100
Yabuki's on the ropes! Yabuki's on the ropes!

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:21.460
Murase's already got a chance to knock him out!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.210
I think I know now.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.000
In the end, he was just acting like a star.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:35.840
Miss...

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:40.920
There were plenty of times like this when he fought me.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.840
There's no need to worry about him.

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.840
Worry? Do you think I am worried?

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:49.850
Well, just watch.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.570
Stop messing with me!

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.270
Joe, you idiot!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:06.530
Guard! Guard!

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.600
Yabuki's not guarding!

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.490
His arms are hanging from his sides!

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.090
Murase's punches are connecting one after another!

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:14.880
Is this a knockdown for Yabuki?

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:16.210
This is ridiculous!

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.380
How on earth did that guy pass the B-class exam?

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:23.880
True, but they say he KO'd the national champion, Inagaki, from that no guard position in that test!

00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:25.330
Th-There it is!

00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:26.910
Th-The Cross Counter!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:38.370
Go to your neutral corner.

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:45.100
How was that, old man? Were you watching?

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:46.880
I got him down with just one punch.

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:49.890
Joe!

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:53.510
Bell!

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.460
Way to go!

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:03.690
World champion!

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:05.670
You're so cool!

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:06.530
Bro Joe!

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:07.700
Bro Joe!

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:07.700
<i>That was cool!</i>

00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:15.880
That was the move he used when he provoked me!

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:19.030
The Cross Counter from hell, Coach!

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:26.150
Now you've taken another step closer to me...

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:28.170
Towards Rikiishi Toru...

00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:48.160
Finally, Joe has done it!

00:23:48.160 --> 00:23:50.560
Joe, you've lived up to everyone's expectations!

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:54.410
The children, Nori-chan, and everyone else are celebrating!

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:58.080
Joe! Let the impression of this victory sink deeply into you!

00:23:59.280 --> 00:24:02.080
Now, for Joe, who has just won his first victory,

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:03.960
which way is tomorrow?
